    <h1>Shingle Roof Cost Guide</h1>

    <!-- Direct Answer Box -->
    <div class="direct-answer">
      <strong>National Average Roof Cost:</strong> For a typical 2,000 square foot single-family home (25 to 28 roofing squares including pitch and waste allowance), a complete shingle roof replacement generally costs between <strong>$8,200 and $14,500</strong> for standard architectural asphalt shingles. Premium materials such as stone-coated metal, synthetic composite, or natural slate range from <strong>$16,000 to over $45,000</strong>.
    </div>

