    <!-- Labor vs Material Split -->
    <h2>Understanding the Labor vs. Material Split</h2>
    <p>
      On an average residential steep-slope roofing replacement, your total contractor bid is distributed across three primary cost categories:
    </p>
    <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-muted); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <li><strong>Labor & Craftsmanship (45% – 60%):</strong> Covers skilled tear-off, decking prep, underlayment rolling, shingle nailing, metal flashing bending, staging, and cleanup.</li>
      <li><strong>Materials & Accessories (35% – 45%):</strong> Encompasses shingles, synthetic underlayment, starter shingles, ridge caps, drip edges, fasteners, and ice-and-water membranes.</li>
      <li><strong>Permits, Disposal & Overhead (10% – 15%):</strong> Covers municipal building inspection permits, roll-off dumpster rental, landfill tipping fees, and contractor insurance liabilities.</li>
    </ul>

